## Statement 1: EditUsingStoredProcedure (AuthorsController.cs)
- Original: DECLARE @rowsAffected INT;EXEC @rowsAffected = [dbo].[uspUpdateAuthorPersonalInfo] @BusinessEntityID, @NationalIDNumber, @BirthDate, @MaritalStatus, @Gender;SELECT @rowsAffected;
- DMS Error: Metadata model creation failed - No objects found
- Manual Conversion: SELECT * FROM bobsbookstore_dbo.uspupdateauthorpersonalinfo(@BusinessEntityID, @NationalIDNumber, @BirthDate, @MaritalStatus, @Gender);
- Conversion Rationale: T-SQL EXEC stored procedure call converted to PostgreSQL function call using SELECT * FROM syntax. Schema [dbo] mapped to bobsbookstore_dbo (matching EF Core ApplicationDbContext configuration). Stored procedure name lowercased per PostgreSQL conventions.

